        "geology": "Triassic schist",
        "hydrology": "The torrential stream of the Dong Cao catchment supplies water to paddy fields located downslope and to a small reservoirs. The flow is permanent.",
        "soils": "According to FAO soil classification (1998), the dominant soil type in the watershed is Ferralic Acrisol with a soil depth of approximately 1m. Some Cambisols and Fluvisols occur along the stream course.The main characteristics of these soils are: a heavy texture with clay contents around 50% and are rather porous with an average bulk density of 1.24 g cm\u00033.",
        "vegetation": "The Dong Cao catchment is mainly covered with shrubland and grasses (52%), fodder grass (Brachiaria ruziziensis; 20%), tree plantation (Acacia mangium, 25%), and very limited annual crops (3%)."
      },
